                <pb facs="0449" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg439"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Waddington to Mr. Hammond.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehall,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I am directed by Secretary Sir George Grey to transmit to you herewith, to be
                    laid before Earl Russell, a copy of a letter which has been received from the
                    Irish government relative to a man named P. H. Finney, who has recently arrived
                    from America, whose object, there is reason to believe, is to enlist men for the
                    American army.</p>


                <xi:include href="d244-a1.xml" xpointer="d244-a1"/>
            </div>
